**Given:**

Principal (P) = ₹2,550

Rate (r) = 8% p.a. compounded half-yearly

Number of instalments (n) = 2

**Formula used:**

Instalment amount (A) = dfrac{P times (1 + (r)/(2 times 100))^n}{dfrac{(1 + (r)/(2 times 100))^n - 1}{(r)/(2 times 100)}}

**Calculations:**

Rate per half year = (8)/(2) = 4%

⇒ Instalment amount (A) = dfrac{2550 times (1 + (4)/(100))²}{dfrac{(1 + (4)/(100))² - 1}{(4)/(100)}}

⇒ Instalment amount (A) = dfrac{2550 times (1.04)²}{dfrac{(1.04)² - 1}{0.04}}

⇒ Instalment amount (A) = dfrac{2550 times 1.0816}{dfrac{1.0816 - 1}{0.04}}

⇒ Instalment amount (A) = dfrac{2757.08}{dfrac{0.0816}{0.04}}

⇒ Instalment amount (A) = dfrac{2757.08}{2.04}

⇒ Instalment amount (A) = ₹1,352

**∴ The correct answer is option 2.**

